{
  "slug": "prodmaster-ai",
  "name": "Prodmaster Ai",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Full-stack engineering ops for Claude Code. One command (/prodmasterai) covers your entire dev lifecycle: orchestrate features into parallel tasks, run 11-phase QA with health scoring, enforce two-pass code review, deploy with dry-run and revert, audit security across 14 OWASP+STRIDE phases, scan dependencies for CVEs, benchmark Core Web Vitals, and run cross-model adversarial review. 31 skills, 4 active safety hooks. The plugin self-improves using velocity data from your completed cycles — no manual tuning needed.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **31 skills**, **1 command** and **4 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (31): `auto-pilot` (Fully autonomous unattended execution -- runs the complete brainstorm->plan->implement->test->PR pipeline without blocking on questions), `auto-pilot-revoke` (Gracefully stop a running auto-pilot session — commits progress, resets concurrency lock, logs revoked status), `benchmark` (Performance regression detection — captures Core Web Vitals, bundle size, request counts, and largest resources), `checkpoint` (Save and restore in-flight task state across plan usage limit resets), `codex` (Cross-model adversarial review — runs Claude and a second AI model independently on the same code, compares results…), `cso` (Security audit — 14-phase infrastructure-first audit covering architecture through STRIDE threat modeling), `decide` (Use when user is at a decision fork -- \"should we do A or B?\", \"what should we…), `dependency-audit` (Audit project dependencies for known CVEs), and 23 more\n- **Commands** (1): `prodmasterai` (ProdMaster AI — reads your project state and acts)\n- **Hooks** (4): `SessionStart`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install prodmaster-ai@claude-community` from `sujithkrishnan-dev/prodmaster-ai`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 31,
    "hook": 4,
    "command": 1
  },
